 type="comment">[MGPRHX73]: 58, n. 24 cites an 18th century work that argues that "gzhon nu tshul khrims" is the real name of 'Dul 'dzin dkar mo (ID:3820) and "shes rab 'bum" that of his student dKar chung ring mo (ID:3821).</note></person><person xml:id="person3827"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'brom ston rgyal ba'i 'byung gnas</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">འབྲོམ་སྟོན་རྒྱལ་བའི་འབྱུང་གནས</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dge bshes ston pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dge bshes ston pa chen po</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dge' bshes ston pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'brum ston rgyal ba'i 'byung gnas</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'brom</persName><birth notBefore="1004-01-01" notAfter="1005-12-31">after 1004 before 1005</birth><death notBefore="1064-01-01" notAfter="1064-12-31">1064</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P2557</idno><idno type="APIS">3827</idno><note type="comment">Celibate householder from the Byang region, chief disciple of Atiśa (ID: 3745) ([Q922IUFM]: 30). &#13;
